From: TB520FU bring-up <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: allow rounded TB520FU LDO12 voltage

The stock PM8550 LDO12 request is 1950000 uV. The mainline pmic5_nldo515
voltage table starts at 320000 uV in 8000 uV steps; its next supported
voltage is 1952000 uV. Exact min=max=1950000 constraints have no selectable
voltage and prevent the RPMh regulator bank from registering. All earlier
regulators in that bank are unwound, and later LDO15/LDO17 consumers,
including the USB repeater, WCN7850 and UFS, remain deferred.

Keep the stock minimum and allow the 2 mV rounding performed by the
hardware. No other regulator limits are changed.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-lenovo-tb520fu.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-lenovo-tb520fu.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-lenovo-tb520fu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-lenovo-tb520fu.dtsi
@@ -167,7 +167,8 @@
 		vreg_l12b_1p95: ldo12 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l12b_1p95";
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1950000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1950000>;
+			/* Stock requests 1.95 V; the NLDO uses 8 mV steps. */
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1952000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 			regulator-allow-set-load;
 			regulator-allowed-modes = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_LPM
